    "Which firmware image each hotspot board takes. scripts/release_build.sh builds one image per board (<id>.bin) from its config, and carries these entries into the release's firmware.json with what each image reports and how to flash it.",
    "id: the board's name in Pi-Star (kept from Pi-Star 4's pistar-modemupgrade); aliases: other names for the same board and image.",
    "gpio (boards on the Pi's serial port): the Raspberry Pi GPIO lines (BCM) on the STM32's BOOT0 and RESET pins, which put it into its serial bootloader; port: the serial port, where it is not the modem port Pi-Star already uses.",
    "Every configs/*.h must be used by a board, so a config added upstream fails the build until it is mapped here."
